"""Render E3 report from saved evidence; no inference calls."""
import json
from collections import Counter
from e3_experiment import DATA,RUN,ROOT,CLASSES,read_lines

def main():
    e=json.loads((RUN/'evaluation.json').read_text());meta=json.loads((DATA/'manifest.json').read_text());div=json.loads((DATA/'diversity.json').read_text());rows=read_lines(RUN/'responses.jsonl');review=read_lines(RUN/'explanation_review.jsonl')
    pct=lambda x:f'{100*x:.2f}%'
    fmt=lambda x:'NA' if x is None else f'{x:.3f}'
    lines=['# E3: cross-user inference with increasing auxiliary knowledge','',
    '## Objective and threat model','',
    'Measure whether increasing labeled observations from other users improves direct pretrained-Qwen inference of a hidden activity. Qwen receives raw binary lists, supplied sensor metadata, 400 real preceding samples, and a fixed 100-sample target. It has no tools, raw IMU values, evaluator labels, subject IDs, filenames, classifier predictions, conversation memory or feedback. No model was trained or fine-tuned.', '',
    'Users 1–7 supply references. The same 14 targets from E2 come from users 8–9, one per subject/activity. These users are unseen in the supplied references, but are repeatedly inspected development subjects, not an untouched final test. Users 10–11 are not used. Histories never cross file boundaries. Each valid export sample is 20 ms apart; this is not a claim about detector decision frequency.', '',
    '## Frozen construction and execution','',
    'K0/K1/K5/K10/K20 contain 0/7/35/70/140 actual 100-bit references. K1 is exactly the seven original E2 User 1 examples. For each class, enumerate nonoverlapping 100-sample training windows inside continuous files. Starting with K1, repeatedly select the candidate minimizing (number already selected from its subject, number from its recording, subject number, relative path, starting index). This prioritizes subject and recording diversity without inspecting bits or inference outcomes. Examples are serialized by rank, then the fixed seven-class order; every smaller set is an exact prefix of the larger set. No naturally identical sequences are removed.', '',
    'K1 uses User 1; K5 uses users 1–5; K10 and K20 use all seven users. K1 deliberately preserves E2 comparability. K5 cannot include seven users per class with only five examples. Provenance, hashes, selection and prompt manifests were frozen before requests. The exact E2 combined prompt/reference set is rerun as a separate 14-request bridge. It is not an auxiliary-count contrast because its prompt differs from E3.', '',
    'The screen has 70 primary requests, 14 bridge requests and two predeclared K20 reversed-reference controls, one target per observable pattern: 86 calls total. The controls use exactly the same example multiset; they assess presentation/order sensitivity, not a clean decomposition of knowledge and context length. No full evaluation or repeated-run expansion was executed. No invalid responses were repaired or retried.', '',
    'Model qwen/qwen3.5-35b-a3b; temperature 0.1; maximum output 600 tokens; reasoning disabled; JSON-object format with strict five-field local validation; parameter-compatible provider routing. No pinned provider or reproducible model sampling seed. Schedule seed 44 rotates conditions across targets. The first planned K20 request was moved to the beginning for a context check; this scheduling exception is logged and not an extra call. Remaining requests used four concurrent workers.', '',
    f'Advertised model context: {meta["model_metadata"]["context_length"]:,} tokens. Largest prompt: {meta["max_prompt_bytes"]:,} UTF-8 bytes, checked conservatively with an output/framing reserve. Actual K20 prompt tokens: {sorted({r["usage"]["prompt_tokens"] for r in rows if r["condition"]=="E3-K20" and r.get("usage")})}. All sequences were sent in full; no silent truncation.', '',
    '## Reference diversity and information limits','', '| Level | References | Unique sequences | Distinct recordings | Training users represented |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---|']
    for k,d in div.items():
        provenance=json.loads((DATA/'reference_provenance.json').read_text())
        recordings=len({p['source'] for c in CLASSES for p in provenance[c][:int(k)]})
        lines.append(f'| K{k} | {d["n"]} | {d["unique_sequences"]} | {recordings} | {d["subjects"]} |')
    lines += ['', 'Every nonempty selected set contains only all-zero and all-one reference patterns. Zeros have Laying, Sitting and Standing labels; ones have Downstairs, Jogging, Upstairs and Walking labels. Each label contributes exactly K examples. The two target/history patterns are also constant. Increasing K adds participants and repeated evidence of ambiguity, but no target-specific distinguishing observations. A fixed mapping from these two inputs achieves at most 4/14 on this balanced screen. This empirical deterministic bound is not a universal cap on a lucky stochastic realization or a claim about other interfaces.', '',
    '## Results','', '| Condition | Valid / planned | Accuracy | Balanced accuracy | Macro-F1 | Motion group, all targets | Mean confidence, valid | Insufficient, valid |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
    for c,v in e['conditions'].items():lines.append(f'| {c} | {v["status_counts"].get("valid",0)}/{v["n"]} | {pct(v["accuracy"])} | {pct(v["balanced_accuracy"])} | {v["macro_f1"]:.5f} | {pct(v["moving_stationary_accuracy"])} | {fmt(v["mean_confidence"])} | {pct(v["insufficient_fraction"]) if v["insufficient_fraction"] is not None else "NA"} |')
    lines += ['', 'Failures count as errors in all-target metrics. Valid-only metrics and matched valid-subset reference baselines are saved in evaluation.json; do not compare surviving subsets as though they were the same target population. The two order-control targets are not a balanced seven-class screen and must not be ranked against the 14-target conditions.', '',
    '| Condition | Prediction counts | Changes vs K0 | Wrong→correct | Correct→wrong |','|---|---|---:|---:|---:|']
    for c,v in e['conditions'].items():
        d=e['contrasts'][c];lines.append(f'| {c} | {json.dumps(v["prediction_counts"])} | {d["changes"]} | {d["wrong_to_correct"]} | {d["correct_to_wrong"]} |')
    lines+=['','## Baselines','','Reference baseline: exact target/reference matching; predict the most frequent label among exact matches, break ties by first occurrence in the frozen reference order. If none match, use the training-majority class. K0 therefore falls back to an evaluator-side training prior not supplied to Qwen; all nonempty conditions have exact matches and use only their supplied examples. It uses only the same references for matching, is not a trained classifier, and never generates Qwen predictions. Reversing the order also reverses this tie-break. Fixed baseline: ones-majority→Walking, otherwise Sitting. Training-majority and prior baselines use users 1–7 labels only. Uniform/prior F1 is from expected confusion, not expected finite-sample F1.','', '| Condition | Reference accuracy / F1 | Fixed accuracy | Majority accuracy | Uniform expected accuracy | Prior expected accuracy |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
    for c,v in e['conditions'].items():lines.append(f'| {c} | {pct(v["reference_baseline"]["accuracy"])} / {v["reference_baseline"]["macro_f1"]:.5f} | {pct(v["fixed_baseline"]["accuracy"])} | {pct(v["majority_baseline"]["accuracy"])} | {pct(v["uniform_baseline"]["expected_accuracy"])} | {pct(v["prior_baseline"]["expected_accuracy"])} |')
    lines+=['','## Confidence, uncertainty and explanation review','', '| Condition | Confidence correct | Confidence wrong | Wrong at confidence ≥0.8 |','|---|---:|---:|---:|']
    for c,v in e['conditions'].items():lines.append(f'| {c} | {fmt(v["confidence_correct"])} | {fmt(v["confidence_wrong"])} | {v["high_confidence_errors"]} |')
    lines += ['', 'Explanation annotations are a provisional qualitative review by the implementation assistant, not an independent human-validated measurement. The review sheet omits target labels/correctness. The reviewer has seen aggregate results, so this is not a fully blinded study. No extra judge API or feedback loop is used. Claims of observed rhythm/intensity, complete stillness, unique posture, invented sample counts, or unsupported reference distinctions are flagged. Explicit arbitrary tie-breaking and qualified plausible alternatives alone are not flagged. Human review is needed before publication.', '', '| Condition | Flagged / reviewed valid explanations |','|---|---:|']
    for c in e['conditions']:
        rs=[r for r in review if r['condition']==c and r['status']=='valid' and r['unsupported'] is not None]
        lines.append(f'| {c} | {sum(r["unsupported"] for r in rs)} / {len(rs)} |')
    lines+=['','## Order control','','```json',json.dumps(e['order_control'],indent=2),'```','','Only two targets, one ordering perturbation and no repeat: any change is suggestive presentation sensitivity; no change does not establish order invariance. Context length and added examples remain confounded in the main K sweep.','', '## Usage, failures and runtime','', '| Condition | Input tokens | Output tokens | Reported USD | Cost / valid |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
    for c,v in e['conditions'].items():
        u=v['usage'];n=v['status_counts'].get('valid',0);lines.append(f'| {c} | {u["prompt_tokens"]} | {u["completion_tokens"]} | ${u["cost"]:.6f} | {"$"+format(u["cost"]/n,".6f") if n else "NA"} |')
    lines += ['', f'Total calls: {len(rows)}. Reported cost: ${sum(v["usage"]["cost"] for v in e["conditions"].values()):.6f}. Wall runtime: {json.loads((RUN/"runtime.json").read_text())["wall_seconds"]:.1f} seconds. Failed responses remain saved and their costs are included.', '']
    for r in rows:
        if r['status']!='valid':lines.append(f'- {r["id"]}: {r["status"]}; finish reason {r.get("finish_reason")}; {r.get("error")}.')
    lines+=['','## Confusion matrices and per-class recall','','Rows: '+', '.join(CLASSES)+'. Columns: same order plus INVALID_OR_MISSING.']
    for c,v in e['conditions'].items():
        matrix=v['confusion_matrix'];recalls=[matrix[i][i]/sum(matrix[i]) if sum(matrix[i]) else None for i in range(7)]
        lines += ['', '### '+c,'','```json',json.dumps({'matrix':matrix,'per_class_recall':dict(zip(CLASSES,recalls)),'by_subject':{s:d['accuracy'] for s,d in v['by_subject'].items()}}),'```']
    lines+=['','## Exact prompt templates','','System:','','```text',meta and json.loads((DATA/'templates.json').read_text())['system'],'```','','User:','','```text',json.loads((DATA/'templates.json').read_text())['user'],'```','','The three placeholders use json.dumps of actual full integer lists/reference objects. K0 references serialize as []. References contain only activity and binary_sequence. Only the reference block changes across the primary E3 conditions. Templates clarify cadence, independent examples and schema uniformly; these changes from the requested draft are not condition-specific. Exact E2 bridge messages are copied byte-for-byte from the saved C111 requests.','','## Interpretation and recommended next experiment','',(ROOT/'reports/e3_interpretation.md').read_text(),'','## Artifacts and reproduction','','All frozen references/provenance, prompts and hidden evaluator labels are in data/e3-screen. Raw predictions, usage, timing, evaluation and provisional explanation annotations are in runs/e3-screen. Prior Stage 1 and E2 inputs/results were hash-checked unchanged. Credentials and data/run directories remain Git-ignored.','','```bash\n# Offline evaluation only; existing annotations are preserved.\n.venv/bin/python e3_experiment.py evaluate\n.venv/bin/python e3_report.py\n```','','prepare and infer reject existing directories to prevent accidental overwrite/reexecution. A new run requires an explicitly separate experiment directory in code; no automatic retries or expansion are supported.']
    (ROOT/'reports/e3_cross_user_auxiliary_inference.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines)+'\n')
if __name__=='__main__':main()
